                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8c9cc17-69ac-3115-83e6-d80e2dd6bec5",
                                        "entry_id": "a8bf750e-8736-35c5-80e9-975b39d366f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A house of worship, especially:",
                                            "A house of worship dedicated to a polytheistic faith."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a74946ca-ffef-4ba7-b06a-ef19ce000556",
                                                "sense_id": "b8c9cc17-69ac-3115-83e6-d80e2dd6bec5",
                                                "text": "The temple of Zeus was very large."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1fc199a-eb2a-4ba5-b69b-6464c9784fdc",
                                                "sense_id": "b8c9cc17-69ac-3115-83e6-d80e2dd6bec5",
                                                "text": "As of October 1968 Lukang, which had a resident population of between 27,000 and 28,000 people, had 39 temples. It is my impression that Lukang has more temples than do most Taiwanese communities of equivalent size. By temple I mean a structure that houses an image, altar, and incense pot, and is freely accessible to the general public. In speaking of the 39 temples of Lukang, I am omitting the numerous small shrines to the unknown dead (Yu Ying Kung), buildings dedicated to ancestors rather than deities (two), Christian churches (four), incense-burner associations that keep their incense pot or image in private homes, and private shrines such as the domestic altars of tang-ki (spirit mediums) or the shrine of the now defunct Ch'üan-chou guild, found in the back room of a drugstore endowed with the guild property.[...]Lukang, seen in comparative perspective, has a lot of temples."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e75657ea-4b6e-3315-9143-596c51c27340",
                                        "entry_id": "a8bf750e-8736-35c5-80e9-975b39d366f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A house of worship, especially:",
                                            "Synonym of synagogue, especially a non-Orthodox synagogue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Judaism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "432ec051-fb17-44c7-9a1d-8766f764f886",
                                                "sense_id": "e75657ea-4b6e-3315-9143-596c51c27340",
                                                "text": "How often do you go to temple?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ec28258-96ad-3891-ab02-fd5128f2f450",
                                        "entry_id": "a8bf750e-8736-35c5-80e9-975b39d366f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A house of worship, especially:",
                                            "As opposed to an LDS meetinghouse, a church closed to non-Mormons and necessary for particular rituals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Mormonism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f28a0ebe-0314-38cd-8388-3ce8f3ffe71f",
                                        "entry_id": "a8bf750e-8736-35c5-80e9-975b39d366f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A meeting house of the Oddfellows fraternity; its members."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f284a422-877b-3f80-b725-3790143e5be9",
                                        "entry_id": "a8bf750e-8736-35c5-80e9-975b39d366f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any place regarded as holding a religious presence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a20336f-142f-3734-8812-eaf74c7a6cb6",
                                        "entry_id": "a8bf750e-8736-35c5-80e9-975b39d366f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any place seen as an important centre for some activity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f85a602e-e1da-4740-82fb-eca9532adfcd",
                                                "sense_id": "1a20336f-142f-3734-8812-eaf74c7a6cb6",
                                                "text": "a temple of commerce; a temple of drinking and dining"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80a65389-4e2b-3d77-ae35-45018f5dbe5e",
                                        "entry_id": "a8bf750e-8736-35c5-80e9-975b39d366f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything regarded as important or minutely cared for."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "557fa06a-42d8-4b8b-825a-ef6de89faed4",
                                                "sense_id": "80a65389-4e2b-3d77-ae35-45018f5dbe5e",
                                                "text": "My body is my temple."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d1921e2-5383-417a-ae14-1e6a3bde3f7a",
                                                "sense_id": "80a65389-4e2b-3d77-ae35-45018f5dbe5e",
                                                "text": "For nature crescent does not grow alone\nIn thews and bulks, but as this temple waxes,\nThe inward service of the mind and soul\nGrows wide withal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05dfd2df-ad68-3ae2-9c7d-b5cb5d7c60d2",
                                        "entry_id": "a8bf750e-8736-35c5-80e9-975b39d366f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A gesture wherein the forefingers are outstretched and touch pad to pad while the other fingers are clasped together."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c646e2c-4a83-467e-b11a-69cebad38fb2",
                                                "sense_id": "05dfd2df-ad68-3ae2-9c7d-b5cb5d7c60d2",
                                                "text": "Again Abdullah listened intently, his eyes closed, his ten fingers forming a temple of his hands in front of him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "temple",
